 "id": "uno_core_demo",
 "package": "uno_core_demo",
 "title": "Uno Core Demo",
 "description": "The light test: the simplest proof that data and signals travel in both directions between a Polari screen and a board. One light on an Arduino UNO can be switched from a Polari screen and from the pushbutton on the board; every change of the light is reported back up as one small record (LightState), so the screen's indicator always follows. This module composes the test's parts by manifest — the firmware (uno-light), the serial link, the cross-domain solution that ties them together and the two Purposes (the screen switches the light, the button switches it) — and works out each part's readiness from the rows themselves, never from a typed-in claim.",
